#EXTM3U
#
# TalTV's free channel list — ships EMPTY on purpose.
#
# This file exists so a first-time visitor with no IPTV subscription still
# has something to try, and so a viewer whose own provider a browser cannot
# reach (docs/design/product-architecture.md §3.1, §9.2) has one playlist
# that can never be CORS-blocked: this one, served from the app's own
# origin rather than fetched across the network.
#
# Two rules, from docs/design/product-architecture.md §9.3 and §14, and
# they are why there are no channel lines below:
#
#   1. Curated by the owner, one entry at a time — never generated,
#      refreshed, or topped up from a community-maintained index. "Free to
#      watch" and "licensed for redistribution" are not the same claim, and
#      a community list mixes both without telling you which is which.
#   2. Every entry is one the owner can personally stand behind as
#      published by its own broadcaster for public viewing. §14 lists
#      "which free channels the owner can stand behind" as a decision that
#      needs a lawyer's eye, not an engineer's, before the first line goes
#      in.
#
# So: this file stays exactly like this — a header and this comment, and
# nothing a parser reads as a channel — until the owner has done that
# review and adds entries by hand. Do not fill it from a scraped or
# community-maintained playlist, however tempting a shortcut that looks
# like. That is the one thing this file must never become.
